# Secrets. Nothing in this project should ever match these, which is the point.
# The application is client-side: no server, no telemetry, and no key that
# belongs to the vendor. There is one deliberate exception -- the optional
# storage summary lets a person configure an endpoint and an API key, and that
# key is written to their user data directory, never here. If any other change
# appears to need a secret in the tree, the design of that change is wrong.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets*
credentials*
!THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md

# Local scratch
_tmp/
scratch/
